## I — Evolution

**Never** by adding systems, managers, providers, architectures, implementations, states, duplicates, temporary fixes.  
**Always** by simplifying · optimizing · automating · preserving.

## II — Before code

Ask (YES/NO): Configuration? State? Providers? Navigation? Services? API? Architecture? **Is the code really wrong?**  
If #8 = NO → **code modifications FORBIDDEN.**

## III — Singularity

Exactly **one** of: Header · Search Engine · Camera Search · Auth · Session · Cookie · User · Callback · Provider · Navigation · Source of Truth.  
Two owners or two implementations → **forbidden**.

## IV — Root cause

One root cause · one smallest fix · preserve greatest architecture.

## V — Deploy

**100/100 only.** 99 or below → NO DEPLOY.

## VI — If it works, do not touch

Auth · Search · Header · Camera Search · Architecture — when PASS, do not reopen.

## VII — No forks

Forbidden: `v2` · Pro · Manager · Engine Pro.  
Allowed: Feature → **optimized** (no new systems).

## VIII — Philosophy

User does less · ROVEXO does more. Remove clicks, questions, pages, API calls, states, providers, complexity until only necessary remains.

## Golden equation

One owner = responsibility = implementation = SSOT = root cause = smallest fix = production gate = canonical implementation.

## Final law

Best fix = **smallest code change** + **greatest architecture preserved**.

## Cursor must never

Violate any principle above · create parallel owners/implementations · deploy below 100/100 · rewrite working modules “because something failed” when configuration/provider is the cause.
